---
import SiteIcon from "../shared/SiteIcon.astro";
---

<section class="container py-5 product-answers-section" aria-labelledby="productAnswersTitle">
  <div class="product-answers-panel mx-auto">
    <div class="product-answers-heading">
      <h2 id="productAnswersTitle">What CogniFocus does</h2>
      <p class="hero-muted-override">
        Short version: CogniFocus protects one focus session at a time, reacts
        when your attention slips, and helps you return before a quick check
        becomes a lost hour.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="product-answers-grid">
      <article class="product-answer-card">
        <span class="product-answer-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <SiteIcon name="mdi:timer-sand" aria-hidden="true" />
        </span>
        <h3>What is CogniFocus?</h3>
        <p>
          CogniFocus is a focus timer and app blocker for Android. You start a
          timed session, choose the distracting apps to block, and let Shield
          protect the session while the Goblin reacts to slips and wins.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="product-answer-card">
        <span class="product-answer-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <SiteIcon name="mdi:shield-lock" aria-hidden="true" />
        </span>
        <h3>How does Shield help?</h3>
        <p>
          Shield reacts instantly when you open a blocked app during a focus session—built for that exact moment you drift into TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, or any app you selected. It's reactive, stepping in before the scroll takes over.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="product-answer-card">
        <span class="product-answer-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <SiteIcon name="mdi:cellphone-link" aria-hidden="true" />
        </span>
        <h3>Where is it available?</h3>
        <p>
          CogniFocus is available now on Android through Google Play. The iOS
          waitlist is open for iPhone updates, and desktop support may follow
          later.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="product-answer-card">
        <span class="product-answer-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <SiteIcon name="mdi:account-heart" aria-hidden="true" />
        </span>
        <h3>Who is it for?</h3>
        <p>
          It is built for students, deep work, ADHD-style distraction patterns,
          app switching, doomscrolling, and anyone who ignores passive timers
          once the session gets boring.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="product-answers-links" aria-label="Related CogniFocus pages">
      <a href="/download.html">Download for Android</a>
      <a href="/ios-waitlist.html">Join the iOS waitlist</a>
      <a href="/faq.html">Read all FAQs</a>
      <a href="/blog/how-to-stop-app-switching.html">Stop app switching</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
